---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage accent="Design" image="/og/pages/about.png"
  kicker="About"
  title={`About ${site.name}`}
  seoTitle="About: Framer templates by Vladimir"
  description={`${site.name} is a small catalog of Framer templates made by Vladimir. Find out who makes them, where to find them on Framer and how to get in touch.`}
  updated="November 6, 2026"
  jsonLd={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href,
    mainEntity: { '@type': 'Organization', name: site.name, url: new URL('/', Astro.site).href, founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: site.author, url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href }, sameAs: [site.framerProfile, ...site.socials.map((s) => s.href)] },
  }}
>
  <h2>Who makes the templates</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is run by Vladimir. Each template is designed and built in Framer and published on Framer Marketplace.
    This site is the catalog: it shows the templates, their pages and live demos, and sends you to Framer to get them.
    Some templates also come as hand-written Astro and Tailwind CSS code, sold through Contra. Nothing is sold on this
    site itself.
  </p>

  <h2>How the templates are made</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Each template starts with one kind of client and what their visitors need to find.</li>
    <li>The design is built in Framer and checked on desktop, tablet and phone.</li>
    <li>The sample content is written for that kind of site, so you can see what belongs on each page.</li>
    <li>Code versions are written by hand in Astro and Tailwind CSS, not exported from Framer.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Templates are edited visually and need no code. Each template page lists the pages it includes and whether it has a
    CMS, so you can judge it before you open Framer.
  </p>

  <h2>Guides</h2>
  <p>
    Vladimir also writes the <a href="/guides/">guides</a> on this site. They cover how to plan, build and publish a
    website with a template.
  </p>

  <h2>Find the work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={site.framerProfile} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vonex Design on Framer</a></li>
    {site.socials.map((s) => <li><a href={s.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.label}</a></li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact and support</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Questions about using or customizing a Vonex template
    are welcome. Please name the template and describe what you see.
  </p>
  <p>
    Account, billing and publishing problems belong to Framer: use <a href="https://www.framer.com/help/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Framer's help center</a>.
    To get started, read <a href="/guides/how-to-use-framer-templates/">how to use a Framer template</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Referral links</h2>
  <p>
    Some links to Framer are referral links. They cost you nothing extra. Details are in the <a href="/terms/">terms</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
